{"c":[{"id":"9f1294f6610d0c4b","sum":"B13-B17: ledger charges text to every window showing it; Jev replays vary ~3 fields; fix generator clock in load tests; acts need an actGrant; Chrome AX late, ignores AXSelectedText; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after builds; Balanced = 4 offers/hour.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d86d11223c1303db","sum":"B13-B14: SnippetLedger charges a text to every window showing it; Jev replays vary ~3 fields, so rerun before reading a delta; socket tests bind to their own HelperServer; load-proof tests fix the generator clock; every stop carries stopReason; dry-run replays with an oracle Jev.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ea5143bf5e6179f1","sum":"B13-B14: SnippetLedger over all windows charges a text to every window showing it; kindless fill fields withheld only on related cuts; live Jev replays vary about 3 fields, rerun before trusting a delta; socket tests bind publish to that test's own HelperServer.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"15d4fcad6f30cb62","sum":"SnippetLedger over model.windows.values() charges a taken text to every window showing it, either way round, and refuses if any is over budget; a kindless fill field is withheld only on cuts of typed values or its label words, never on any cut (B13).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075125Z-769f076b2b26d50b","text":"SnippetLedger(windows) charges a taken text to every window that shows it, either way round (line inside the text, or text inside a line); refuses when any of them is over budget. Build it over model.windows.values(), never just the source window (B13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T075154Z-10f895f4b8d309e7","text":"A fill field whose label names no kind is withheld when a cut took a typed value or a cut conversation left out a line sharing its label words; withholding it on any cut blanked Name on the fill desk (unrelated team chat always cut) and lost the first-look offer (B13 live-final).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"be073912f9f26071","sum":"Live Jev replays vary by about 3 fields run to run (24-27 of 78, B13): rerun before reading a delta. Socket tests bind publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, or a late 'stopped' leaks into the next test (B14).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075211Z-5ac7a437648ff4d5","text":"Live replay noise: the same code gave 24, 26, 27 and 25 of 78 on 'sources in Messages' rule on (B13); pre-ask withholding is deterministic, so differences under about 3 fields are Jev answering differently. Rerun part with --variants/--rules/--fixes before reading a delta.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100918Z-34fd442f4a978ffa","text":"Socket test harnesses must bind the helper's publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, not the reassigned server variable: an earlier test's run timed out 5 s later and its 'stopped id-1' reached a later test's host (B13's flake, fixed B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7d2825e282ce0f8d","sum":"B14: fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) in load-proof tests; names are withheld only on namesCut; every stopped taskProgress carries stopReason; try a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev before a live replay.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b51bc99b3aa533a8","sum":"B14: load-proof tests fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (find exposed ones with a wall clock jumping 1 s per read); a name field is withheld only on namesCut, since counting names prose mentions blanked Full name on Messages sets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100918Z-d51f417a758957f9","text":"Tests whose answers must not depend on CPU load fix the generator's budget clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (candidates.ts); find exposed tests by making the wall clock jump 1 s per read and rerunning the suite (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-90979468cad825fe","text":"Names are a fill kind (kinds.ts NAME_TERM): a field that takes a name is withheld only when namesCut (name-like lines or a contact line's names kept out, a partway cap/clock stop, cutAll); counting names that prose mentions blanked Full name on every Messages set (B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d0f5d3ab6d535ae7","sum":"B14: a stopped taskProgress carries stopReason (stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase); before a live replay, run a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev to see withholding and wrong fills for free.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100919Z-9bbdea6cd359a808","text":"A stopped taskProgress must carry stopReason: executor progress() refuses 'stopped' at type level and stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase so the exported JSON Schema states the rule (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-aefa98c201821a3a","text":"Before a live replay, copy live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev (gold if offered, else a name-like decoy) to see withholding and wrong fills for free; B14's copy is ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b14/oracle/oracle-replay.ts.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"09651b924661b23f","sum":"B15-B17: acts need an actGrant, revoked by any pause/stop; Chrome builds web AX late and ignores AXSelectedText(Range); background WKWebView drops writes; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after fixture builds; event cards judge the last typed sentence; Balanced = 4 offers/hour.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d8e5e429dbcf056a","sum":"B15 (updated B22): the reader acts only under an actGrant from an accepted offer, revoked at once by any pause, stop or take over; Chrome builds web AX trees late and ignores AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes; the walk check catches drops.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"166b843e5f81c9fe","sum":"B15: any pause, stop or take over revokes the act grant at once (fakes refuse acts without one only under enforceGrants); Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds late, so wait for the form's fields in the model before acting.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124042Z-0ff3662999b3099a","text":"A stop or takeOver revokes the task's act grant at once, so a write still on its way is refused and the run ends as stopped by you; test fakes (FakeApp, SocketReader) refuse acts without a grant only when enforceGrants is set.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124042Z-b3569a4cf63d6bee","text":"Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds after the reader asks for it: wait until the form's fields are in the screen model before acting, or the first plans stop with target-not-found (B15 explore run).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ead499ab30c4256f","sum":"B15: the reader acts only under an actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s, monotonic) from an accepted offer. Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs but ignores AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes; the executor's walk check catches each drop.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124106Z-598a6c678d777d69","text":"caret-screen acts only under a helper actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s max, monotonic); --act-pids is for fixture tests. Only accepted offers get grants (Executor.run opts.grant); a consumer runPlan never does, so the product refuses it (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124106Z-77698db11d4c9d42","text":"Real targets (B15): Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs, front or back, but answers AXSelectedText ok and changes nothing; WKWebView in background-only caret-fixture drops value and insert silently; TextEdit takes all. The executor's walk check caught each drop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"20ef30b80edf7d92","sum":"B15-B17: Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes (insert refused); caret-fixture can't take the front from T3; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after fixture builds; event cards judge only the last typed sentence (empty body first); Balanced = 4 offers/hour (eager for a fifth).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d7fa6d069180cfdc","sum":"B15-B16: Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes on web inputs, so insert is refused there; caret-fixture cannot take the front from T3; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after any swift build that changes the fixture, or evals run the old one.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T135628Z-a8acf778077d3916","text":"Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes on web inputs (selection stays 0+0), so the insert fallback is refused there; and caret-fixture's 'activate legacy' cannot take the front from T3 Code, only from apps the eval launched (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T145037Z-c765ed8386dc228d","text":"Evals exec CaretFixture.app, a copy of caret-fixture made by apps/screen-reader/scripts/bundle-fixture.sh: rerun it after every swift build that changes the fixture, or the eval runs the old one (B16 lost two planner cases to an 08:33 bundle).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1148a14e8f8ea414","sum":"B17 tests: an event card judges only the last finished sentence typed (send an empty body first, then a body ending in the sentence); Balanced allows 4 offers an hour, so a test needing a fifth pop-up sets level eager first.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-3aee21889eca1d38","text":"Event cards judge only the last finished sentence of what is typed: a test body must end with the event sentence and arrive as a change (empty body first), or no attend question is asked (B17 privacy session).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T191104Z-a560fe18d0d7ba87","text":"Balanced allows 4 offers an hour (settings.ts LEVELS): a socket test that needs a fifth pop-up sends settings level eager first, or the gate silently holds it (B17).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f0617985abdd2b3d","sum":"B17-B21: About fills need both whose-asks (0.5); planner asks named fields only. swift test: 2 GiB heavy lease. Skill undo resets clean count; pid posts reset HIDIdleTime; background fixture ignores posted clicks; Electron evals drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2bd6c65512b6f7b3","sum":"B17-B19: typed About values fill only when both asks say the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5; planner asks only named fields; wrongKind needs a host sentence. Heavy lease 2 GiB for swift test. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell (override setters to reformat).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"28beb5cb41b23736","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev scores typed About Name/Email 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; such a value fills only when both asks call it the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16/20, 0 wrong). Planner asks only fields the instruction names; wrongKind needs a host sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0bc8adb9f0371420","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev picks typed About Name/Email at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; prompt rewordings did not help. Such a value fills only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16 of 20, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-ec0243a8194ed7a7","text":"Live Jev picks a typed About Name/Email in both asks but at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 fill cutoff, on standalone forms (B17 held-out: 1-3 of 17 filled, 0 wrong); three prompt rewordings on a dev set did not raise it (evidence/screen/b17/dev).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-3b718a56937eb180","text":"A typed About value fills only when both asks also answer the field's whose-details question as the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (fill.ts); a memory cutoff alone needed 0.6 on B18's dev set and filled 4-7 of 20, the whose question 12 of 20, held-out live 16 of 20 with 0 wrong.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8ece4134d4c0c551","sum":"B18 planner: asks only about fields the instruction names unless asksToFillForm (no field named: nothingToDo); PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind, which v2/host's exhaustive planError switch needs a sentence for.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-c901993f6e9aca54","text":"PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind (B18, kinds.ts misfit: whole address in City, email in Phone); v2/host's AskCaret.planError switch is exhaustive and needs a sentence for it at its next merge of v2/screen.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-d62444babaa7f479","text":"The planner asks only about fields the instruction names (relevance, or namesShortLabel for To/Cc/ID) unless asksToFillForm; an instruction that names no field, like 'msg: ...', now gets nothingToDo (B18 traded that for no unrequested writes).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"94b0d9540949ad9f","sum":"Ask 2 GiB heavy leases for swift test (peaks 0.44 GB). B19 evals: copy new values each time, set offersPerHour and actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; override cell objectValue/stringValue and accessibilityValue() to reformat.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7a2abedd05327146","sum":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks 0.25-0.44 GB RSS; ask a 2 GiB lease (6 GiB is refused below ~17 GiB free). Routine evals must copy new values each time, or the closed earlier destination's text is credited as the next source and predictions miss (B19).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-db99791d758fef32","text":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks at 0.25-0.44 GB RSS (/usr/bin/time -l, B18); a 6 GiB lease estimate is refused below ~17 GiB free disk, so ask for 2 GiB.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-01ce9c46dd16673e","text":"Routine evals must copy new values each occurrence: with static source text the closed earlier destination's recent text is credited as the next source, the shape changes and predictions miss (B19; caret-fixture --windows forms, stdin form next).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"496e4b113a33f3ef","sum":"B19: real-time skill evals set offersPerHour (Eager 8/h) and writeElsewhere actIfApproved. caret-fixture AX writes land in the NSTextField cell; to reformat, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and accessibilityValue() (setAccessibilityValue never fires).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-69bacc9b74bdc91c","text":"Real-time skill evals need Helper offersPerHour (Eager allows 8 offers an hour) and writeElsewhere set to actIfApproved, since a background-only fixture is never the user's window and ask first caps promotion (B19).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e6e14bbcf17c1b8d","text":"caret-fixture: AX value writes land in the NSTextField's cell and AX reads return a cached value; to reformat input, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and the field's accessibilityValue() -> String? (setAccessibilityValue never fires) (B19).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"69b2a79eea55f5b4","sum":"B19-B21: undoing a skill run resets its clean count; posted clicks reach only a --foreground caret-fixture; pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime (log last post); a closing window can arrive fieldless; drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for Electron; non-key WKWebView: focusValue.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"22bae55a2a60fd23","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count; a per-pid listen-only tap sees clicks posted to that pid; background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click (use --foreground); pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime, so GUI evals log their last post.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d9542f01119cf37d","sum":"B19-B20: undoing a skill run resets its clean count. A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid (global monitor and session tap do not); a background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click, --foreground (accessory) does.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e77935deee83e487","text":"Skills (B19): undoing a skill run resets its clean count, so a fixture forced-mismatch run with no Tab needs ten more clean runs after run 11's undo. Live Jev's first naming ask fell under NAME_CUTOFF 0.5 in 7 of 9 tries; the reworded retry picked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-795f3dcc958c0f2c","text":"A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid; the global NSEvent monitor and a session tap do not (B20, 6 of 6 vs 0 of 6). A background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click and cannot hit-test a covered window; --foreground (accessory) does both.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e619089820dda277","sum":"B20: input posted to a pid resets HIDIdleTime like a person's, so GUI evals record their last post (scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them. TextEdit cannot host a routine: one text area, no positions, one value per field.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T234914Z-993bc2a42fa75599","text":"Input posted to a pid (CGEventPostToPid) resets HIDIdleTime like a person's (B20: 196 s to 0.3 s); GUI evals that post input record their last post (helper/scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them as 'user back'.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-ac2ee9392ce81473","text":"TextEdit cannot host a B19 routine: a shape is (source template, part, destination template) with no positions, a document is one text area, values copied from list lines share one source template, and engine.plan writes one value per field (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f76396784bf60827","sum":"B20-B21: a closing window can reach the model fieldless; routines use last-seen places. Evals starting Electron drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE. A non-key WKWebView writes AXValue to the focused field (reader: focusValue). Shadow keys are hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a097a19063cce23e","sum":"B20: a closing window can reach the model without its fields before its close, so routines place late edits from where elements were last seen; the agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, so an eval starting Electron must drop it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-5758654235cf32d7","text":"A closing window (Chrome tearing down its page, a Send that closes it) can reach the model without its fields before its close; routines place late edits and presses from where elements were last seen, or Caret's verified runs score as misses (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T004204Z-584e781bcb96f4a6","text":"The agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for its children; an eval that starts Electron must drop it or Electron runs as plain Node and cannot require('electron') (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"70fc0cfcbac83876","sum":"B20-B21: a non-key WKWebView applies an AXValue write to the focused field, so the reader focuses a web field first (focusValue); the shadow store keeps keys only as hashes, so real-day-replay counts approximate and memory.sqlite routine rows are exact.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-9249ce81a51a9397","text":"WKWebView in a window that is not key applies an AXValue write to whichever field has focus (none: dropped; another: overwritten). The reader focuses a WebKit web field first (focusValue): 3/3 landed, no raise or activation; typing or paste to the pid land 0/3 (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-03e29f7fee084743","text":"The shadow store keeps element keys only as hashes, so an offline replay cannot recover templates or positions; scripts/real-day-replay.ts counts are approximations both ways; memory.sqlite routine rows are the faithful count (B21).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
